# Gated workflow (must follow)

## 1) Review first (no edits)
- Before changing anything, scan the relevant parts of the app to understand current behavior, conventions, and impacted files.
- Summarize findings and list the files likely to be touched.

## 2) Propose a todo list and wait for approval (no edits)
- Produce a clear todo list with small steps.
- Do not start implementing until the user explicitly approves the todo list (or asks to modify it).

## 3) Implement file-by-file with an approval gate
- Only modify **one file per iteration**.
- After updating a file, stop and ask the user to approve that file’s change.
- Do **not** edit any other file until the user approves (or requests changes) for the current file.

## 4) Proceed sequentially until the todo list is done
- If approved, move to the next todo item and the next file.
- If rejected, revise only the same file and request approval again.
- Repeat until all todo items are completed.
